course: dictionary
lesson: 10683
title: Unpopular: not liked by many
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word unpopular is made from un- (not) and popular (liked by many people). So unpopular means not liked by many people, or by most people. When you meet it, ask: who is not liking this, and how many?
explain: «Courage means doing what is right even when it is scary or unpopular.» The clue is "even when". Doing what is right is good, but some people may still dislike it, so it is unpopular with them. Doing the right thing and being popular are not always the same.
explain: An unpopular decision, rule or idea is one that many people disagree with. «Judges ... rule fairly even when it is unpopular» means a judge may make a fair choice that many people do not like. A person can also be unpopular if few people like them.
fact: Unpopular means not liked by many people or by most people.
fact: An unpopular decision, rule or idea is one many people disagree with.
fact: An unpopular character in a story has few friends or is disliked.
fact: Useful phrases: «unpopular with», «deeply unpopular», and «an unpopular decision».
fact: The opposite of unpopular is popular, which means liked by many people.
exercise: «Courage means doing what is right even when it is scary or unpopular.» What does unpopular mean? | *Not liked by many people | Very old and worn out | Very loud and noisy | Quick to finish a task
exercise: A ban on football at break might be an unpopular rule. What does that mean? | It is the only rule in the school | *Many people disagree with it | It has no effect on anyone | Everyone loves it and asks for more
exercise: What is the opposite of unpopular? | Unhappy | Careful | Quiet | *Popular
test: «The new rule to stop all snacks was deeply unpopular.» What does deeply unpopular mean? | *Disliked by a great many people | Liked by the whole team | Hard to read | Kept secret from everyone
test: Which sentence uses unpopular correctly? | The sun was unpopular and shone all day | *The new rule was unpopular, so many children were upset about it | The cake was unpopular, so everyone asked for more of it | I was unpopular because I drew a picture of a dog
exam: Is it always wrong to do something that is unpopular? | Only if a judge says so | Yes, anything unpopular is wrong | *No, doing what is right can still be unpopular
